  "merits": "Breaking the fast with dates: This act doubles the reward of the prayer to four hundred folds.\n\nAllahumma laka sumto: One who says this supplicatory prayer will be awarded, by Almighty Allah, the rewards of all those who observe fasting on that day.\n\nAllahumma Rabban Nur al-Azim: This supplicatory prayer also brings about a great merit.\n\nForgiveness at the first bite: Forgiveness of Almighty Allah is the reward of those who say this imploration. A Hadees reads: Almighty Allah releases from Hellfire one million persons at the last hour of every day in Ramazan; therefore, pray Him to include you with these released ones.\n\nFeeding fasters: Concerning this, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is reported to have said, “Verily, anyone who offers food for a faster in Ramazan will have the same reward that is decided for the faster without having any amount of his reward reduced and will have the same reward of acting good deeds according to the power of that food.”\n\n‘Allamah al-Hilli, in al-Risalah al-Sa’diyyah, has narrated that Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said, “As for any believer who feeds another believer with a single bite of food in Ramazan, Almighty Allah will decide for him the reward of manumitting thirty believing slaves and will decide to respond to his prayers.”\n\nDua for forty years of forgiveness: Sayyid ibn Tawus has mentioned that if one says a supplicatory prayer each night in Ramazan, his sins of forty years will be forgiven."
